## What SOUFFLE changes relative to EMTG

| Area | Change |
|---|---|
| Inner-loop NLP solver | **Uno** (open source, MIT) replaces SNOPT as the default solver |
| Solver abstraction | `NLP_interface` (abstract) + `NLP_solver_factory` replace direct use of `SNOPT_interface` |
| Uno integration | `SouffleApi` (runtime dynamic loading) + `Souffle_interface` (model/bound/Jacobian mapping) |
| Build | `SOUFFLE_WITH_SNOPT` (default **OFF**), `SOUFFLE_WITH_UNO`, `SOUFFLE_UNO_ROOT`, `SOUFFLE_DEFAULT_SOLVER` |
| Packaging | self-contained distribution (bundled Python + PyEMTG GUI + Uno runtime) |

**No SNOPT code or binary is required, included, or linked in the default build.** The
files `src/InnerLoop/SNOPT_interface.*` and `src/InnerLoop/snoptProblemExtension.h` are
EMTG's own NOSA-licensed source that *calls* SNOPT; they are compiled only when
`SOUFFLE_WITH_SNOPT=ON`. SNOPT itself is commercial software and is **not** distributed
here — you must obtain it separately and under your own license if you enable that path.

---

## Third-party components

| Component | License | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Uno** | MIT | <https://github.com/cvanaret/Uno> — not vendored; obtain separately |
| **Boost** | Boost Software License 1.0 | not vendored; obtain separately |
| **CSPICE** | § see `EMTG_NOSA_License.pdf` | part of the EMTG distribution |
| **GSL** | GNU GPL v3 | part of the EMTG distribution |
| **wxPython** (for the PyEMTG GUI) | wxWindows Library Licence | not vendored; see `BUILDING.md` |
| **SNOPT** | commercial | **not distributed**; required only if `SOUFFLE_WITH_SNOPT=ON` |

Redistributors of a binary build are responsible for complying with the licenses of the
components they bundle (in particular the Intel Fortran runtime redistributables that a
SNOPT-enabled build would pull in — the default SNOPT-free build does not).

